# Wave W17-N (Scorch Path): scorch rock — heat-darkened banded rock of the through-road’s walls: dark ember-brown strata with one heat-bright band running at shoulder height where the mountain’s fires keep warming it (design: a warm cave lit by its own fires, ember-red and black). The Scorch’s own wall — it converts the shipped volcrock WALL register on this map only (on Routes 112/113 volcrock is dressing and stands byte-preserved); split from Gloom’s near-black gut bands by the heat band’s warmth.
